# Project: EZ Wonders — kids' numeracy game platform

## Repo map (read first — "monorepo" is misleading)

- Workspace root `d:/Phaser/games` **IS the frontend** (Vite + React). `src/games/`
  is the games *domain of the frontend*, not a backend.
- Backend = `D:\K1 games project\server` (Node/Express + Mongoose), a **sibling
  outside the workspace**. Tools can't read it by default and edits there aren't
  part of this repo. Never assume a server change is testable from here.
- Docs drift (this file included). For API truth, **read the actual server file**
  (`server.js`, `server/models/*.js`) before trusting any spec.
- Leave alone unless asked: `dist/`, `_sout.log`, `server/IMPLEMENTATION_PROMPT.md`,
  `server/SETUP.md`, `server/logPlaySession.js` (stale copy of the frontend file;
  nothing imports it, so edits there change nothing).
- Don't re-explain React/Tailwind/Express basics. If unsure a helper exists,
  **read the file** — recent consolidations removed near-duplicates and re-adding
  one would undo that.

## Stack (frontend)

react 19, react-router-dom v7, zustand v5 (+persist), tailwindcss v4 via
`@tailwindcss/vite` (NO `tailwind.config.js`; theme is CSS `@import "tailwindcss"`
+ `@theme`), motion (`import { motion } from 'motion/react'`), phaser v4,
@dnd-kit/* (admin drag-reorder), react-confetti, use-sound, react-helmet-async,
clsx + tailwind-merge, react-qr-code, jspdf + html-to-image (student badge only),
react-use.

## Stack (server)

Express + Mongoose. **Auth is NOT JWT/session-based** — every write endpoint
re-validates a code against the DB per request, via `requireTeacher` /
`requireAdmin` / `requireClassAccess` middleware in `server.js`.

## Domain model (classId-scoped)

**`classType` is DEPRECATED.** Kept on `ClassInfo` (`enum ['k1','k2']`) and
`GameAccess` only so legacy docs validate and a bad migration can roll back. It
drives nothing. Never key new code on it.

- **`ClassInfo`**: `classId` (unique), `className`, `classAlias` (short label),
  `classYear`, `classCode` (globally unique login code, sparse), `isPublic`
  (public = join with name + classCode; private = per-student code), `active`
  (soft-retire, never delete), `image` (null → render a placeholder),
  `classType` (deprecated). Teacher list is **derived** by querying `Teacher`, never
  stored on the class.
- **`Teacher`**: `code` (unique), `name`, `classId` (**null for the global admin**),
  `role: 'teacher' | 'admin'`, `active` (soft-deactivate so historical stats still
  resolve). One admin code, from the `ADMIN_CODE` env var via a boot migration. No
  seeded teacher list.
- **`Student`**: `studentId` (server UUID, not Mongo `_id`), `classId`, `fullName`,
  `nickname`, `group` (freeform label, no behaviour), `code` (6-char, unique,
  sparse → drives `/p/:code` auto-login), plus `mergedInto`/`mergedAt`/`mergedBy`.
  Merged-away rows are **never deleted**, so a merge stays reversible.
- **`GameAccess`**: classId-scoped — one row per `{classId, gameKey}` under a
  **partial** unique index (`partialFilterExpression: { classId: { $exists: true } }`).
  The partial filter is load-bearing: legacy `classType`-only rows are kept for
  rollback and must not collide. Fields: `added` (opted in from the catalogue — a
  class only sees games it added), `unlocked`, `shiny`, `order`, `unlockAt`,
  `updatedBy`, `updatedAt`.
- **`PlaySession`**: one row per completed round — `game`, `playerName`,
  `studentId`, `classId`, `stars`, `totalRounds`, `peakStreak`, optional
  `elapsedSeconds`/`mistakes`, `mergedFrom`, `completedAt`, `device {kind, os,
  browser, userAgent}`.
- **`PlayerMerge`**: name-based merge groups within one class — `primaryName`,
  `members[]`, `active`. The authoritative merge record (merges mostly target
  "light" kids with no Student row).
- **`SystemConfig`**: singleton `_id:'system'` — `maintenanceMode`,
  `maintenanceMessage`, `maintenanceEndsAt`; polled live.
- **Legacy fallback** `classId: 'k12026-pny'` when the client classId is missing
  (`LEGACY_CLASS_ID` in `logPlaySession.js`).

## Scheduled unlocks

`GameAccess.unlockAt` (Date, nullable) is the only field the feature added. A row
with `unlockAt` set is **always `unlocked: false`** — the schedule is a promise to
flip it later, not a parallel state.

- Unlock-early clears `unlockAt`; removing or re-adding a game also clears it.
- Due unlocks apply **lazily on read** via `resolveDueUnlocks()` inside
  `getGameAccessRows()`. **There is no cron** — a schedule still fires correctly
  after the server slept through the exact minute.
- Every read path returning game rows MUST go through `getGameAccessRows()`
  (auto-unlocks first). Never query `GameAccess` directly on a read path.
- `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/schedule` sets `unlockAt`: past time → 400,
  already-unlocked → 409. It must stay **above** `/api/game-access/:gameKey`
  (Express matches in registration order).
- The same endpoint **cancels** when sent `unlockAt: null` (clears the field, game
  stays locked; 404 if nothing was scheduled). A cancel is deliberately NOT a past
  time — "unlock it now" is a different, destructive intent.
- A module-scope `pendingUnlockCache` lets the sweep be skipped when the next due
  time is comfortably future (re-checked ≥ every 30 s). It *skips work*, never
  serves truth — Mongo is re-read every request. **Any write that can change
  `unlockAt` MUST call `invalidateUnlockCache(classId)`** (schedule, lock/unlock,
  catalogue add/remove all do).

## Auth model

- `POST /api/code-lookup` classifies a code into exactly one: `teacherCode` |
  `adminCode` | `studentCode` | `classCode`. A bare `classCode` is not a session —
  it branches the login flow to a name prompt (public class) or a student-code
  prompt (private class).
- `isTeacher` / `isAdmin` in zustand are **UI state only, not a security
  boundary** — every write endpoint re-validates server-side.
- **`requireTeacher`**: view own class info, manage own roster, view/edit own
  class's games. Scoped to own `classId`.
- **`requireAdmin`** (`requireTeacher` + `role === 'admin'`, else 403): class
  create/update, `PATCH /api/system/config`, admin stats routes.
- **`requireClassAccess`** — the class-write workhorse: an admin may target **any**
  classId, a teacher only their **own**. Gates all `GameAccess` writes and the
  per-class student merge/unmerge/delete routes. (Corrects older "game-access is
  admin-only" — a teacher manages their own class's games.)
- The admin's `classId` is **null** → any component resolving a class-scoped thing
  must handle the no-class case (e.g. `NextGameTimer` self-hides; `GameAccessGate`
  lets teachers/admins through *before* its loading gate, or an admin would spin
  forever).
- Login: `NameGate.jsx` posts to `/api/code-lookup` (and `/api/student-login` for
  the light path); the server returns the full identity. **No client-side
  hardcoded teacher-code mirror** — `src/teacherCodes.js` was deleted because the
  frontend copy drifted from the DB and locked out new teachers. Do not
  reintroduce one.

## Frontend gating flow

`@/auth/NameGate.jsx` (whole-app entry, also wraps every game) captures a code, or
a name + public class code, and persists **only the credential** in
`@/auth/playerStore.js`. `@/auth/GameAccessGate.jsx` wraps each game and re-checks
per-game unlock via `useIsGameUnlocked`. Both re-fetch independently if data isn't
loaded for the current classId. New game routes need **both gates, in this order**:
`NameGate` → `GameAccessGate` → game. Teachers/admins pass `GameAccessGate` before
its loading gate.

`@/auth/playerStore.js` persists only `{code, name, mode}` — the credential needed
to re-resolve identity from the DB on every load. Names, classIds and roles are
**runtime-only**, so removing a student or changing a code signs that device out on
its next validation. Bump the persist `name`/`version` **only** to force a global
re-login (that's what `version: 3` was); either logs every device out. The legacy
`k1weekly-player` key is removed on boot. `AuthBootstrap` (in `main.jsx`) awaits
`hydrate()` before render, so a signed-in user never flashes the login screen.

## Source layout (`src/`) — `@/` alias → `src/`

Alias configured in `vite.config.js` + `vitest.config.js` + `jsconfig.json` (all
three must agree). Cross-folder imports use `@/`; relative imports are only for
siblings in one folder.

```
app/    main.jsx (entry + routes), index.css, aurora.css
api/    apiClient.js (the ONE fetch/timeout source), logPlaySession.js,
        students.js, classInfo.js, systemConfig.js, deviceFingerprint.js
auth/   playerStore.js (persists only {code,name,mode}), NameGate.jsx,
        GameAccessGate.jsx, MaintenanceGate.jsx
games/  registry.js  ← THE game list; gameAccess.js (unlock store; re-exports the
        catalogue), gameIcons.js, levels.test.js, <slug>/ (one folder per game)
pages/  BetaHome.jsx (home at /), GameAccessPanel.jsx, GameAccessPage.jsx,
        StatsPanel.jsx, TeacherOnboarding.jsx + teacherOnboardingContent.js,
        StudentLogin.jsx, StudentBadge.jsx, PublicLanding.jsx, WeeklyGoals.jsx,
        MissionHeroes.jsx, NextGameTimer.jsx
phaser/ BaseGame.jsx, BaseScene.js, BasePreloadScene.js, config.js, common/
pwa/    pwa.js, PwaBadges.jsx, staleChunkRecovery.js
ui/     cn.js, brand.js, GameIcon.jsx, BrandLoader.jsx, ErrorBoundary.jsx,
        RotateHint.jsx, confirmDialog.jsx, FeedbackButton.jsx, ContactStrip.jsx
seo/    seo.jsx
```

- `@/api/apiClient.js` — **the single source of truth for `API_BASE`, `withQuery`,
  `fetchWithTimeout`, `requestJson`, `postJson` and `ApiError`.** Never redeclare
  an API origin or roll a new timeout — that drifted before (12s / 15s / none) and
  the missing one hung app boot, since `AuthBootstrap` blocks render on `hydrate()`.
- `@/games/registry.js` — every game, once (key, slug, opaque 5-digit route, term,
  progressKey, meta, lazy `load`). Drives the catalogue, the routes and the
  homepage prefetch; `GAME_CATALOG`/`GAME_KEYS` and `StatsPanel`'s `GAME_LABELS`
  all derive from it.
- `@/games/gameAccess.js` — the classId unlock store used by Home /
  `GameAccessGate`, plus class-scoped mutators used only by the panel. Re-exports
  `GAME_CATALOG` / `GAME_KEYS`. Also `mergeRows(rows)`,
  `nextScheduledGame(games)` / `useNextScheduledGame()`, `useGameByKey()`,
  `formatUnlockCountdown()`. The read store seeds from a localStorage cache
  (`ezw.gameAccess.v1`, 7-day max) so the grid paints before a cold Render wakes;
  12 s timeout, aborts superseded requests. Legacy classType-scoped mutators still
  exist but are **unused**.
- `@/api/logPlaySession.js` — `logPlaySession({game, ...})` called by every game on
  completion (`POST /api/plays`; reads classId with legacy fallback, attaches a
  device fingerprint, failures only `console.warn`), plus `fetchStats` /
  `fetchSummary` / `fetchPlaysPage` / `fetchLeaderboard` / `fetchWeeklyMission` /
  `fetchAdminClassStats` / `deletePlayerGame`. Slugs: `game1`…`game9`,
  `bonusGame1`.
- `@/app/main.jsx` — entry: builds routes straight from `GAME_REGISTRY`, runs
  `AuthBootstrap`, and holds **two** `ErrorBoundary`s (app-level + per-route) so a
  failed lazy chunk can't blank the app. Wrap new top-level surfaces in one.
  **Never hand-add a game route here.**
- `@/pages/BetaHome.jsx` — the real home at `/`. Large; holds the SVG `Icon`
  library, card gradients, the aurora backdrop layers, and `SwitchPlayerButton`
  (the shared-device "not you?" affordance — it exists, don't add another).
- `@/pages/GameAccessPanel.jsx` — the admin/teacher panel. Role-split tabs:
  admin = **Classes · Catalogue · Stats · Settings** (pick a class, manage its
  games inline); teacher = **Games · Catalogue · Students · Stats · Settings**, all
  scoped to their own classId. Reorder via @dnd-kit; a clock button opens
  `ScheduleUnlockDialog`; "Confirm changes" batches only the deltas.
- `@/pages/TeacherOnboarding.jsx` (`/teacher-onboarding`) — the public teacher
  guide. **Copy and imagery live in `teacherOnboardingContent.js`**
  (`ONBOARDING_SECTIONS` + `ONBOARDING_GIFS`), not in the component. An empty GIF
  string renders the "coming soon" placeholder; a broken URL falls back via
  `onError`. Listed in `PUBLIC_DURING_MAINTENANCE` in `MaintenanceGate.jsx`.
  **Never rename the content file to `teacherOnboarding.js`** — it would differ
  from the component only by case, and on a case-insensitive filesystem an
  extension-less `./TeacherOnboarding` import can resolve to it (→ "lazy element
  type is invalid").
- `@/phaser/common/` — `audioState.js` (mute + bg music), `numbersVoice.js`,
  `speech.js`, `sceneAssets.js`, `starProgress.js`, `uiHelpers.js`.
- `@/ui/cn.js` — the **only** file importing `clsx` / `tailwind-merge`.

## Server endpoint contract

All return `{ error: '...' }` with non-2xx on failure. "RL" = rate-limited.

Auth/codes: `POST /api/code-lookup` (RL; classifies a code into one identity kind),
`POST /api/teacher-login` (RL; `{code}` → identity | 401), `POST /api/student-login`
(RL; public-class light login), `GET /api/student-login/:code` (auto-login via
`/p/:code`), `POST /api/codes/check` (namespace availability).
Classes: `GET /api/classes`, `GET /api/classes/:classId`, `POST /api/classes`,
`PUT /api/classes/:classId`, `PATCH /api/classes/:classId/public`,
`PATCH /api/classes/:classId/code`.
Students/identities (teacher-scoped to own class): `GET|POST /api/students`,
`PUT|DELETE /api/students/:studentId`; `GET /api/classes/:classId/identities`
(roster ∪ distinct play names + merges); `GET|POST /api/classes/:classId/students`,
`PUT|DELETE .../students/:studentId`; `POST .../students/merge`,
`POST .../students/:studentId/unmerge` (pass the literal `name` as `:studentId` for
a light identity); `DELETE /api/classes/:classId/identities/:name` — deletes a
**name-only ("light") identity** by removing its play sessions (that history is the
only thing making it exist); 409 if the name still matches a roster student (delete
the student instead). Defensive: matches `classId` against both the URL param and
the actor's own classId.
Game access (writes require `requireClassAccess`): `GET /api/game-access?classId=`
(read; auto-unlocks first; ownership enforced only when a `teacherCode` is given;
**no hardcoded game-key allowlist** — the DB is truth); `PUT /api/game-access/order`
(must equal the currently-added set); `POST|DELETE /api/game-access/:gameKey` (add
from catalogue, starts locked, clears stale `unlockAt` / soft-delete `added:false`,
resets lock/shiny/`unlockAt`); `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/shiny`;
`PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey/schedule`; `PUT /api/game-access/:gameKey`
(lock/unlock; **unlocking clears `unlockAt`**). Route order: `/order`,
`/:gameKey/shiny` and `/:gameKey/schedule` **must stay above** `/:gameKey`.
Plays/stats: `POST /api/plays` (RL; falls back to the legacy class if classId is
absent client-side), `DELETE /api/plays` (one player's records for one game),
`GET /api/stats` (teacher `$facet`: totals + per-game breakdown), `GET /api/summary`
(teacher code → paginated `{rows,total,page,limit,hasMore}`; `classId` + `playerName`
→ plain array), `GET /api/plays` (paginated sessions), `GET /api/leaderboard`,
`/api/leaderboard/:game`, `/api/player/weekly`, `/api/weekly-mission`,
`GET /api/admin/stats/classes`, `/api/admin/stats/classes/:classId`.
System: `GET|PATCH /api/system/config` (maintenance; read public, write admin),
`POST /api/feedback` (RL), `GET /api/ping`, `/api/health`.

**Rate limits apply ONLY to unauthenticated/abuse-prone routes:** `code-lookup`,
`teacher-login`, `student-login`, `plays`, `feedback`. Do **NOT** add limits to
authenticated write paths — a whole class can legitimately burst `/api/plays`, and a
per-IP cap would throttle everyone behind one school NAT. Per-IP limits need
`app.set('trust proxy', 1)` (Render's TLS terminator).

## Mongoose / Mongo gotchas

- Nested subdocument keys must avoid a literal `type` (Mongoose reads it as a
  type-declaration shorthand) — hence `PlaySession.device.kind`, not `.type`.
- **Schema field changes do not migrate indexes.** A Mongoose edit alone won't drop
  or rebuild an existing index; do it explicitly, then call `syncIndexes()`.
  (`GameAccess`'s unique key moved classId → classType → classId, each with an
  explicit drop.)
- `unlockAt: null` **sorts below every Date** — the due-unlock filter must be
  `{ $ne: null, $lte: now }`; a bare `$lte` matches every unscheduled row.
- Boot migrations run in the `mongoose.connect().then()` chain **before
  `app.listen`** and must be self-guarding/idempotent (check the absence of the new
  field / presence of the old) so redeploys don't redo or corrupt. Order:
  `ensureSystemConfig` → `migrateAdminRole` → `migrateClassFields` →
  `migrateGameAccessToClassId` (drops the old unique index first, `syncIndexes()`,
  keeps the classType rows) → `migrateStudentCodes` / `auditCodeConflicts` →
  `syncIndexes()`.
- Adding an enum value (e.g. a role): update the model enum **and** the boot replay
  path that applies it to existing documents.
- Connect options `bufferCommands: false` + a tight `serverSelectionTimeoutMS`
  avoid silent hangs on Render/Atlas cold starts.

## Conventions

- Comments explain **why**, not what — a short rationale above non-obvious logic.
- Extend the existing zustand store / API helper rather than creating a parallel
  one: one store per domain, one thin fetch-helper per API concern, **one**
  `apiClient.js`.
- Env: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (frontend, default `http://localhost:4000`),
  `MONGODB_URI`, `ADMIN_CODE`, `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (backend).
- **Frontend `.env` IS COMMITTED and must stay committed.** It holds only the
  public API origin and is the only place a deployed build reads it (no host-side
  frontend env). Untracking it makes production fall back to `localhost:4000` —
  every request fails and the browser reports a **CORS error** pointing at the
  server instead of the missing config. Private values → `.env.local` (gitignored)
  or the backend host's env.
- **`cn()` lives in `@/ui/cn.js`** — import it, never redefine; `clsx` /
  `tailwind-merge` are imported there only.
- **Fonts: Fredoka only, loaded once in `index.html`.** Never add a component-level
  Google Fonts `<link>` — it can't start until that lazy chunk runs, so the font
  competes and text reflows on arrival. `.font-heading` / `.font-body` are declared
  in `src/app/index.css` and are both Fredoka; do **not** re-declare them in a
  component's inline `<style>` (that duplicate was removed from ~15 files). Nunito
  is not loaded and must not be referenced.
- **`localStorage` keys** are namespaced and shared where the concept is shared.
  Mute uses one key (`ezw-muted-v1` in `@/phaser/common/audioState.js`) — mute is a
  property of the player, not of a game. Never give a game its own mute key.
- Chrome pages share the `aura-*` theme (`src/app/aurora.css`) — don't hand-roll
  new sky/white themes.
- Phaser games use Phaser's native input; `@dnd-kit` is DOM-only. `react-confetti`
  is for React level-complete overlays; Phaser games use `this.sound`, not
  `use-sound`.

## Performance / platform

- `vite.config.js` sets `manualChunks` as a **function** — Vite 8 bundles with
  rolldown, which rejects the Rollup object form ("manualChunks is not a function").
- `vite-plugin-pwa` ships the service worker. Phaser (~1.4 MB) is excluded from
  precaching via `globIgnores` and cached at runtime on first real play, because
  eager precaching would tax every visitor including those who never open a game.
  The API is never cached (`navigateFallbackDenylist`). DevOptions are disabled in
  dev so a stale module graph can't be served.
- `public/site.webmanifest` is hand-maintained and linked from `index.html`;
  `VitePWA` uses `manifest: false` so it doesn't generate a second one.
- **Canonical/robots are per-route** via `src/seo/seo.jsx`: add a public route to
  `INDEXABLE_ROUTES` there **and** to `public/sitemap.xml`, or it's marked `noindex`
  and pointed at the root canonical.

## The "next game" banner

`NextGameTimer.jsx` is **schedule-driven, not calendar-driven** — the old "new game
every Friday" cadence is gone; there is no default cadence.

- Renders **nothing** when the class has no pending schedule; callers gate it on
  `useNextScheduledGame()` so the surrounding layout collapses cleanly. The Weekly
  Champions leaderboard always shows regardless.
- Names the soonest `!unlocked && unlockAt` game and counts down in
  days/hours/mins/secs, then calls `fetchGameAccess()` at zero so the server applies
  the unlock and the banner either rolls on or disappears.
- Teachers see it too (schedule preview); the admin has no class, so it self-hides.
- Panel control: the clock button in each locked game row opens
  `ScheduleUnlockDialog`. Scheduled rows show an "⏰ Unlocks ..." badge. The button
  is hidden once a game is unlocked. Once a schedule exists, a separate cancel
  button (in the row and the dialog) clears it while leaving the game locked.
- `GameAccessGate` uses `formatUnlockCountdown()` to show a coarse "Ready in 2d 4h"
  on a scheduled game instead of the generic "isn't out yet / ask your teacher".

## Adding a new game — one folder + one registry entry

`GAME_REGISTRY` in `src/games/registry.js` drives the routes (`app/main.jsx`), the
catalogue (`GAME_CATALOG`) and the homepage prefetch — so nothing else is edited.

1. Create `src/games/<slug>/`. Phaser = `GamePage.jsx` + scene files; React = a
   single `Game.jsx`. Both default-export the page component.
2. Add ONE `GAME_REGISTRY` entry: unique `key`, `slug`, opaque unique 5-digit
   `route`, `term`, `progressKey`, the card `meta`, and
   `load: () => import('@/games/<slug>/…')`. That's the entire wiring step.
3. Wrap in `NameGate` → `GameAccessGate` (correct `gameNumber`/`gameLabel`) — copy
   an existing `GamePage.jsx`.
4. Call `logPlaySession({ game: '<slug>' })` on completion; `game` must equal that
   entry's `progressKey`.
5. Audio via `addMuteButton` / `ensureBgMusic` from `@/phaser/common/audioState`,
   never a per-game copy.
6. It appears once an **admin/teacher adds it to a class** from the Catalogue.
7. Ensure `title`, on-screen heading and catalogue `label` all agree, and no other
   game already uses that name (a duplicate is invisible in the panel and has
   shipped a mismatch before).
8. Optional icon: `public/game-icons/<slug>.png` + one line in
   `@/games/gameIcons.js` (root-relative `/game-icons/…` so cache headers and the
   service worker both cover it).

**Never** re-add a `lazy()` import or `<Route>` in `main.jsx`, and never edit
`GAME_CATALOG` directly — both derive from the registry, and hand-editing is how
the route, card and unlock list drift apart. No server change or redeploy is needed
for a new game.

## Testing

Vitest for pure logic (`npm test`). No DOM/E2E suite. Prefer testing pure functions
— `mergeRows`, `nextScheduledGame`, `formatUnlockCountdown`, the round generators in
the `levels.js` files, and the device fingerprint. `vite build` and `npm run lint`
run in CI; both must pass (lint = 0 errors).

## CI supply-chain gate

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs, in order: `npm ci` → **`npm audit --audit-level=high`**
(blocking) → `npm run lint` → `npm test` → `npm run build`. All five must pass.

- The audit gate can fail on a **transitive** dependency nobody edited — an advisory
  simply landed (this happened 2026-09-30: `brace-expansion` via `filelist`, and
  `fast-uri`). The fix is `npm audit fix`; it updates **`package-lock.json` only**, so
  it never changes a pinned version in `package.json`. Commit the lockfile.
- Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) opens weekly npm + GitHub-Actions bumps
  (minor/patch grouped) so this usually arrives as a PR before CI breaks.
- Do not lower the audit level or add `|| true` to unblock a run — the auth credential
  lives in localStorage, so a vulnerable dep is an exfil path.
- `npm test` currently fails in this environment for an unrelated Vitest runner issue
  (all suites, including untouched ones) — that is environmental, not a code failure;
  lint + build are the local gates to trust.

